From 1deb50f88ac11697d35b25558209b813cc938c6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:12:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Peanuts Nova: CPU-side build for the Exynos 1580 (Galaxy A56)

On the Galaxy A56 the frame waits for the CPU: Tears of the Kingdom runs
31 ms a frame with 20 ms of GPU work.

- android/host: the whole host at -O2 (it was the Mac host's -O1), the
  replay (dm/gfx/vk_android) at -O3 (was -O2).
- build.gradle: -PnxCpu=<cpu> passes -mcpu to every native library
  (cortex-a720+nosve for the A56: Armv9.2, LSE atomics in place of LL/SC
  loops between the replay and the encoder).
- vka_auto.h: DM_VK_PUSH_DELTA on RADV (its push set keeps its words
  between pushes of one layout, radv_init_push_descriptor_set), and
  DM_VK_CS_WARM on RADV and Samsung's Xclipse driver.
- Use fast cores on by default: the replay keeps the fastest core.
- Overlay and DeviceStats: the CPU cap is read on the cluster the game's
  threads run on (at 75 % of the top clock or more), not on the policy
  with the most cores, which is the small cores' on a 1 + 3 + 4 CPU.
